From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 16:00:19 +0200
Subject: arm64: dts: mediatek: mt8395-radxa-nio-12l: set UFS
 lanes-per-direction

The UFS link on this board trains a single lane per direction, but the
ufshci node omits lanes-per-direction, so ufshcd-pltfrm assumes the
default of two. Since commit e72323f3b09f ("scsi: ufs: core: Configure
only active lanes during link") that mismatch is fatal:

  ufshcd-mtk 11270000.ufshci: Tx lane mismatch [config,reported] [2,1]
  ufshcd-mtk 11270000.ufshci: link startup failed -67
  ufshcd-mtk 11270000.ufshci: probe failed -67

One lane is what the link actually negotiates; U-Boot's UFS driver
reports the same on this board:

  [RX, TX]: gear=[3, 3], lane[1, 1], pwr[FAST MODE, FAST MODE], rate = 2

Declare the actual lane count so link startup succeeds again.

Signed-off-by: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8395-radxa-nio-12l.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8395-radxa-nio-12l.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8395-radxa-nio-12l.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8395-radxa-nio-12l.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8395-radxa-nio-12l.dts
@@ -1167,6 +1167,7 @@ &uart1 {
 };
 
 &ufshci {
+	lanes-per-direction = <1>;
 	vcc-supply = <&mt6359_vemc_1_ldo_reg>;
 	vccq2-supply = <&mt6359_vufs_ldo_reg>;
 	status = "okay";
-- 
Armbian

